course: dictionary
lesson: 10889
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Violet can be a colour, a flower, or even a description of a person. The words around it tell you which one you need. Ask yourself: is this something I can see, or is it a person?
explain: «The sky turned violet as the sun went down.» Here violet is a colour, a bluish-purple, because the sky is changing shade. Try your meaning in the sentence: the sky turned bluish-purple as the sun went down. It still makes sense.
explain: «Violets grow in the grass in early spring.» Now violet is a small plant with purple, blue or white flowers. Grass and spring are clues that it is a flower, not a colour.
explain: Informal words are clues too. «A shrinking violet» is a very shy person, not a flower. In the phrase «violet seas, tawny sands», violet paints a picture of a deep colour, and tawny (golden brown) sits beside it.
fact: Violet is a bluish-purple colour, and as a noun it is also a small plant with purple, blue or white flowers.
fact: Violet is the last colour of the rainbow: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.
fact: Ultraviolet light lies beyond violet, and it can burn your skin, so wear sun cream on bright days.
fact: In art, violet is made by mixing blue and red.
fact: A «shrinking violet» is an informal way to describe a very shy person.
exercise: «The sky turned violet as the sun went down.» What colour is violet here? | Pale yellow like sand | Bright green | *Bluish-purple | Dark brown, like a tree trunk
exercise: «Violets grow in the grass in early spring.» What is a violet in this sentence? | *A small plant with purple, blue or white flowers | A very shy person | A bright colour in a paint pot | A kind of bee
exercise: Which colour is the last one in the rainbow? | *Violet | Green | Yellow | Red
test: «She was a shrinking violet at the party and hardly said a word.» What does shrinking violet mean? | A tall flower in a garden | *A very shy person | A loud singer | A person who paints the sky
test: «The violet carpenter bee chews tunnels in wood for its nest, and it is one of Europe's biggest bees.» What is a violet carpenter bee? | A flower | *A kind of bee | A tree | A purple shade only
exam: Ella says violet is always a colour. Is she right? | *No, violet can be a colour, a flower or a shy person, and the context shows which | No, violet is only ever a flower | Yes, but only in paint | Yes, violet is always a colour
